0266-negroni-wlan-qmi-wlfw: Wi-Fi level 6 (negroniwlan=6), QMI WLFW client, steps 18-24.
New bsd/dev/negroni_wlan_qmi.{c,h}: a generic QMI TLV encoder/decoder (our code, from the wire
format: 7-byte header, TLVs, nested string/array prefixes; unknown TLVs skipped, mandatory TLVs
checked) and the WLFW sequence of cnss2 (qmi.c:133/271/410/499/950/1103, main.c:509):
IND_REGISTER (fw_ready, fw_init_done, request_mem, fw_mem_ready, cal_done), HOST_CAP (cnss2 fields:
num_clients 1, bdf/m3/m3_cache support, cal_done 0, build type 2, feature list 0x5), REQUEST_MEM_IND ->
contiguous segments (<= 64 MiB total, 36-bit) -> RESPOND_MEM (ath11k 0-segment retry once),
FW_MEM_READY_IND, CAP (chip/board/soc/fw version/build id log), BDF_DOWNLOAD regdb.bin (type 4) then
bdwlan.elf / bdwlan.eNN (type 1 ELF) in 6144-byte segments, M3_INFO, FW_INIT_DONE_IND (max(negroniwlan_to, 10 s)).
New bsd/dev/negroni_wlfw_tables.h: the field tables, one source line (v01.c / v01.h) per field.
Every response: TLV 0x02 result/error logged and checked. Failure path: quiesce, then free once.
Details: patches/xnu/README-wifi.md "0266".

